1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,979
Warm water in one place
can bring rain far away.

2
00:00:04,617 --> 00:00:08,291
Normally, trade winds push
warm Pacific water west.

3
00:00:08,867 --> 00:00:11,500
But in El Niño,
those winds weaken.

4
00:00:12,533 --> 00:00:16,602
So the warm water slides back
east, toward the Americas.

5
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,431
That moves the jet stream
south of its usual path.

6
00:00:21,033 --> 00:00:24,246
So the Gulf Coast and
Southeast tend to get wetter.

7
00:00:24,867 --> 00:00:28,065
And the northern states
tend to be warmer and drier.

8
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:33,098
This one has about an 80% chance
of staying strong through March.

9
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,940
Loaded dice. Not a promise.
